{"name":"Soothsayer","hex":"#8092bc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soothsayer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who attempts to predict the future, using magic, intuition or intelligence; a diviner.","A mantis (Mantodea spp.)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soothsayer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Divination","blocks":[{"text":"Divination is the attempt to gain insight into a question or situation by way of a magic ritual or practice. Using various methods, throughout history, diviners have been providing answers to querents by reading signs, events, or omens, often claiming to receive insight through supernatural agents such as spirits, gods, god-like-beings or the \"will of the universe\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Rhumsiki_crab_sorceror.jpg/330px-Rhumsiki_crab_sorceror.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divination"},{"title":"Fortune-telling","blocks":[{"text":"Fortune-telling is the spiritual practice of predicting information about a person's life. The scope of fortune telling is in principle identical with the practice of divination. The difference is that divination is the term used for predictions considered part of a religious ritual, invoking deities or spirits, while the term fortune telling implies a less serious or formal setting, even one of popular culture, where belief in occult workings behind the prediction is less prominent than the concept of suggestion, spiritual or practical advisory or affirmation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/%D0%A8%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE_%D0%A2._%D0%93._%281841%29_%D0%A6%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0-%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg/330px-%D0%A8%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE_%D0%A2._%D0%93._%281841%29_%D0%A6%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0-%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortune-telling"},{"title":"Soothsayer (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Soothsayer (1808–1827) was a British Thoroughbred racehorse and sire best known for winning the classic St Leger Stakes in 1811. Bred and originally trained in Yorkshire, he won the St Leger on his third racecourse appearance when still unnamed. He was later sold and trained for the remainder of his racing career at Newmarket where he won a valuable sweepstakes in 1812 and a match race against the Derby winner Phantom in 1813. He later became a successful breeding stallion, siring two classic winners and being the Leading sire in Great Britain and Ireland in 1819. He was later exported to Russia where he died in 1827."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Soothsayer_%28horse%29.jpg/330px-Soothsayer_%28horse%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soothsayer_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeptameron_magic_circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Divination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg/500px-Divination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Divination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg/1280px-Divination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Divination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg/500px-Divination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Display on divination, featuring a cross-cultural range of items, at the Pitt Rivers Museum in Oxford, England ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADivination_display_at_the_Pitt_Rivers_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/ChickenDivination.jpg/500px-ChickenDivination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/ChickenDivination.jpg/500px-ChickenDivination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Russian peasant girls using chickens for divination; 19th-century lubok.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChickenDivination.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Safavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_%28Book_of_Omens%29%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg/500px-Safavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_%28Book_of_Omens%29%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Safavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_%28Book_of_Omens%29%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg/1280px-Safavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_%28Book_of_Omens%29%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Safavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_%28Book_of_Omens%29%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg/500px-Safavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_%28Book_of_Omens%29%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joseph Enthroned. Folio from the \"Book of Omens\" (Falnama), Safavid dynasty. 1550. Freer Gallery of Art. This painting would have been positioned alongside a prognostic description of the meaning of this image on the page opposite (conventionally to the left). The reader would flip randomly to a place in the book and digest the text having first viewed the image.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASafavid_Dynasty%2C_Joseph_Enthroned_from_a_Falnama_(Book_of_Omens)%2C_circa_1550_AD.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Enrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg/500px-Enrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Enrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg/1280px-Enrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Enrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg/500px-Enrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Fortune Teller, by Enrique Simonet (1899; canvas; Museo de Málaga), depicting a palm reading","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnrique_Simonet_-_La_buenaventura.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Anon-The_screene_of_fortune_here_behold-Early-Harl5937271-E2_4_240_-p1.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Anon-The_screene_of_fortune_here_behold-Early-Harl5937271-E2_4_240_-p1.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Anon-The_screene_of_fortune_here_behold-Early-Harl5937271-E2_4_240_-p1.tiff/lossy-page1-1280px-Anon-The_screene_of_fortune_here_behold-Early-Harl5937271-E2_4_240_-p1.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","s